  "executive_briefing": "As of mid-2026, global corporate tax regimes and trade frameworks are undergoing structural shifts defined by operational minimum taxes, evolving trade barriers, and digital compliance mandates. Over 140 jurisdictions are enforcing OECD Pillar Two global minimum tax regulations to establish baseline effective tax rates. Concurrently, international trade compliance is marked by legal uncertainty as the U.S. Supreme Court prepares to review the legality of executive tariffs enacted under the International Emergency Economic Powers Act (IEEPA). Regionally, ASEAN economies continue to calibrate competitive statutory rates with targeted reliefs, such as Singapore's corporate tax rebates, while digital tax administration accelerates globally as countries establish hard timelines for Peppol-based continuous transaction controls stretching through 2031.",
